Z||000008||LVMY88||09-16-2001||09:47 PM||||Fiero5 and 87V6GT did mine for me on Mothers day. Turned my notchback into a fastback and it looks awesome!<BR>There are lots of little things you need to do when swapping, like changing some of the pins in the new wiring harmess to match up the brake lights and so on.<P>Marian<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Marianssig.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000009||sqoach||09-16-2001||10:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LVMY88:<BR><B>Fiero5 and 87V6GT did mine for me on Mothers day. Turned my notchback into a fastback and it looks awesome!<BR>There are lots of little things you need to do when swapping, like changing some of the pins in the new wiring harmess to match up the brake lights and so on.<P>Marian<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, I mean the rear fascia (bumper). To change all the moldings, you also need to change the front and rear fascias. Only the fastbacks had smooth molding with the ground f/x. I like your car though. Pretty neat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
